    "excerpt": "Homocysteine is a blood marker influenced by vitamin B12, folate and other metabolic pathways. Testing may help assess selected nutritional or inherited metabolic questions, but is not a routine cardiovascular screen.",
    "content": "**Quick answer:** Homocysteine is a blood marker influenced by vitamin B12, folate and other metabolic pathways. Testing may help assess selected nutritional or inherited metabolic questions, but is not a routine cardiovascular screen. Kidney function, medicines and specimen handling affect results. QXL must confirm the collection and separation protocol, assay, current quote and report time before an eligible Bengaluru appointment.\n\n**Also known as:** total homocysteine, plasma homocysteine, tHcy\n\n## What is the Homocysteine test used for?\n\n- Selected investigation of suspected vitamin B12 or folate deficiency when additional biochemical evidence is needed.\n- Specialist evaluation or monitoring of suspected homocystinuria or other inherited metabolic disorders.\n- A defined clinical question in which the result is expected to alter management; avoid routine cardiovascular screening.\n\n**Conditions it helps investigate:** Disorders of homocysteine metabolism\n\n## What does the test measure?\n\n- **Total homocysteine:** Includes measured homocysteine forms after assay processing; an indirect, nonspecific marker of one-carbon metabolism.\n\n## How is it tested?\n\nTotal homocysteine may be measured by enzymatic, immunoassay or chromatographic/mass-spectrometric methods. Cells continue to release homocysteine after collection, so validated separation and transport procedures are important. QXL must confirm its actual method, specimen and handling SOP.\n\n## Sample and preparation\n\n**Specimen:** Venous blood; serum or plasma suitability must be confirmed for the actual QXL assay.\n\n- Confirm whether QXL requests fasting and the specified duration; recent dietary intake may affect the result.\n- Disclose B-vitamin supplements, medicines, kidney disease and recent nutritional treatment.\n- Arrange collection only when prompt processing under QXL’s validated protocol is available; do not improvise specimen cooling or separation at home.\n\n| Specimen detail | What to confirm |\n|---|---|\n| Volume | Confirm minimum and paediatric volume with QXL test master. |\n| Container | Use the collection tube or container specified by the actual QXL test SOP. |\n| Stability | Confirm separation deadline, validated transport temperature, cold-chain and stability window with QXL. |\n| Rejection | QXL must confirm identification, specimen quality, quantity and transport acceptance criteria. |\n\n## How are the results interpreted?\n\n- An elevated result can accompany B12, folate or other vitamin-related abnormalities, but is not specific for any one deficiency.\n- Kidney impairment and other clinical factors can raise homocysteine.\n- A raised result alone does not establish an inherited disorder or predict an individual cardiovascular event.\n\n**Reference interval:** Use the method, units and context-specific interval or decision limits on the actual laboratory report; no universal numeric normal range is substituted.\n\n## What are the limitations?\n\n- It cannot replace direct vitamin assessment, clinical evaluation or targeted metabolic investigations.\n- Routine population testing for heart disease risk is not recommended; lowering a number does not necessarily improve cardiovascular outcomes.\n- Delayed separation and unsuitable handling may produce an artefactual elevation.\n\n## How does it compare with other tests?\n\n- Methylmalonic acid can help address a B12-specific question, but kidney function also affects it; it is not interchangeable with homocysteine.\n- B12, folate, blood count and clinical findings are interpreted together rather than using homocysteine alone.\n\n## Notes for referring clinicians\n\nState the clinical question, relevant treatment and specimen timing. Discuss unexpected or discordant results with the laboratory before changing management.\n\n## Price, report time and home collection\n\n- **Price:** Request the current QXL quote, included components and any collection charges.\n- **Report time:** Confirm test-specific QXL reporting time, its starting point, working-day conditions and any referral transit before collection.\n- **Home collection:** Ask QXL to confirm Bengaluru pincode eligibility, test suitability, collection timing and whether the visit is free.\n- **Processing:** QXL verification pending: performing laboratory, platform and in-house versus referral status.\n- **Report review:** Appropriately qualified laboratory authorisation is required. Ask QXL whether a separate report-discussion appointment is available. This content has not received medical sign-off.\n\nCall [+91 9964 639 639](tel:+919964639639) or [WhatsApp QXL](https://wa.me/919964639639) to confirm the current quote, preparation and collection slot.\n\n## Frequently asked questions\n\n### Is this a routine heart attack screening test?\n\nNo. Routine cardiovascular risk screening with homocysteine is not recommended for everyone.\n\n### Can high homocysteine show a vitamin deficiency?\n\nIt may support further investigation, but several vitamin pathways and other conditions can affect it.\n\n### Does high homocysteine prove B12 deficiency?\n\nNo. Folate and other factors, including kidney function, may also increase the result.\n\n### What is homocystinuria?\n\nIt is a group of inherited metabolic disorders requiring specialist assessment; a raised result alone cannot establish the diagnosis.\n\n### Why is sample handling important?\n\nOngoing cellular release after collection can increase measured homocysteine if separation and transport are delayed.\n\n### Should I fast or stop B vitamins?\n\nConfirm fasting instructions and disclose supplements. Do not change prescribed treatment without advice.\n\n### Should I take vitamins simply to lower the result?\n\nTreatment should address the identified cause and your clinical needs; do not self-treat from one number.\n\n### Can QXL collect the sample at home?\n\nOnly if the validated processing and transport requirements can be met. Confirm suitability, charges and reporting time before booking.\n\n## Related test guides\n\n- [Fasting Insulin & HOMA-IR Test in Bengaluru](/blog/fasting-insulin-homa-ir-test-bengaluru-guide)\n\n## Sources\n\n- Tietz ninth edition, PDF pages 1427 and 1430: B12/homocysteine pathways, nonspecific elevations and pre-analytical sensitivity.\n- MedlinePlus homocysteine guidance cross-checks routine cardiovascular screening limits and nutritional/metabolic use.\n\n*Educational information only; not a diagnosis or a substitute for a doctor’s advice.*",
